# WordPress

Apply only when working with WordPress themes, plugins, or headless WordPress integrations.

## Security (non-negotiable)

- Sanitize inputs; escape outputs.
- Validate capabilities/permissions for protected operations.
- Use nonces for form and AJAX actions where applicable.
- Never commit or expose authentication secrets, application passwords, or tokens.

## APIs

- Prefer standard WordPress APIs over custom reinvention.
- Use REST API or GraphQL according to the project’s established choice.
- Reuse existing fetch/normalization utilities in headless setups.
- Separate backend concerns (CPTs, fields, permissions) from frontend presentation.

## Scope

- Do not modify unrelated WordPress content, settings, or plugins.
- Keep schema/content-model changes minimal and documented.
- Account for missing fields and API failures in consumers.
